  "title": "Wangari Maathai",
  "summary": "Wangari Maathai (1940–2011), born in Nyeri, Kenya, became in 1971 the first woman in central and eastern Africa to earn a PhD, according to EBSCO. In 1977 she renamed Envirocare the Green Belt Movement, which promotes poverty reduction and conservation through tree planting. In 2004 she became the first African woman to win the Nobel Peace Prize.",
